    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d910">

                <pb facs="1031" n="1019" sameAs="frus:frus1943v03/pg1019"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00114A Pacific War/396: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harrison</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bern</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-04-07">April 7,
                        1943</date>.<lb/>[Received April 7—8:43 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2179. American interests Far East. Department’s 2868, December 19.<anchor n="15"
                        xml:id="d910-f1"/> Legation’s 6222, December 30.<anchor n="16"
                        xml:id="d910-f2"/> Swiss Legation Tokyo telegraphs following reply from
                    Japanese Government: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“In principle Japanese Government not opposed sending correspondence and
                            packages to American prisoners of war, civilian internees Japan and
                            territories under Japanese control but cannot authorize neutral ships
                            enter waters where military operation taking place.</p>
                        <p>However, if American Government disposed send Vladivostok correspondence
                            and packages for American internees either by Soviet <pb facs="1032"
                                n="1020" xml:id="pg1020"/> ship or by land across Siberia Japanese
                            Government ready examine possibility relieving present situation.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harrison</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
